Once an XMLHttpRequest’s decoded bytes pass the response’s Content-
Length, Ladybird reports the length as unknown, as Blink and WebKit do:
Blink’s XMLHttpRequest::DispatchProgressEvent() and WebKit’s XML-
HttpRequest::didReceiveData() both make an event length-computable only
while the received length is at most the expected content length, and
report a total of 0 otherwise. Gecko instead reports the channel’s own
progress, in encoded bytes, against the Content-Length.
